===City Under Siege===
Several Grunts from [[Team Magma]]{{sup/3|R}}/[[Team Aqua]]{{sup/3|S}} can be seen loitering around the city. One of them even orders you not to go near the cave in the cove. Another blocks the waterway leading to {{rt|124|Hoenn}} as he trains a group of Pokémon.

===Pokémon Trainer Fan Club===
The [[Pokémon Trainer Fan Club]] is located to the east of the Pokémon Center. Inside, members meet to discuss popular Pokémon Trainers and [[Gym Leader]]s. After you have entered the [[Hall of Fame]], several members then announce themselves as fans of yours, as well.

===Cove Lily Motel===
The [[Cove Lily Motel]] can be found in the southeast part of town. With the presence of [[Team Magma]]{{sup/3|R}}/[[Team Aqua]]{{sup/3|S}}, most tourists have decided to stay away. The man who runs the motel can be seen on the first floor, watching a TV program. He wonders aloud if finding a cute Pokémon to use as a mascot will help draw in more patrons.

After entering the [[Hall of Fame]], return to find the staff of [[Game Freak]] on the second floor. The group is touring the [[Hoenn]] region, and has just recently checked into the motel. Speak to the Game Designer after completing the [[List of Pokémon by Hoenn Pokédex number|Hoenn Pokédex]] to receive a [[Diploma]] celebrating the achievement!

===Pokéblock Master's house===
The house to the west of the motel belongs to a couple and their four children. The woman calls herself a master of [[Pokéblock]]s, and offers to teach you how to make the best candy.

:''"If you look at Pokéblocks, you should see that they are rated on how they feel. The lower the feel rating, the better it is. Don't forget this! A good Pokéblock has a low feel rating and a high level. A Pokémon can eat more good Pokéblocks than ordinary ones, too. And this is important. If you want to make smooth Pokéblocks, use different kinds of Berries. Don't be stingy—the kinds of Berries affect the smoothness of Pokéblocks. And another thing. The more people blending Berries, the smoother the Pokéblocks. That's why you should talk to other people and make Pokéblocks together."''

