===Lilycove Museum===
[[File:Lilycove Museum 1F RSE.png|thumb|Lilycove Museum, 1F]]
[[File:Lilycove Museum 2F RSE.png|thumb|Lilycove Museum, 2F]]

The [[Lilycove Museum]] stands in the northwest part of town. It holds a collection of statues and sculptures, and a wide array of paintings. There is no charge for admission. The first floor houses the main exhibit hall. A special gallery is located on the second floor.

=====The Curator's Request=====
The curator can be found in front of the stairs to the upper floor. He is happy to see someone as young as you visiting the museum, and asks if you have viewed their collection of paintings yet. Agree, and he recognizes you as a Trainer, and asks if you are interested in paintings, as well. Agree again, and he escorts you to the second floor.

The man points out the empty spaces on the walls. He would like to display something different here than the classical works on the lower floor, and decides to look for modern and vibrant paintings instead. Seeing that you are young and well-traveled, he points out that you will likely encounter such artwork, and asks that you obtain the artist's permission to display it here. If you win a Master Rank [[Pokémon Contest]] with a score of at least 800 points, you will be approached by an artist. He explains that he has just completed a painting that may even look good in a museum, at which point you will direct him here. Collect one painting for each of the five Contest categories, and the curator will reward you with a {{DL|List of decorations in Generation III|Glass Ornament}} for your [[Secret Base]].

===Move Deleter's house===
The first house to the east of the Department Store belongs to a man known as the [[Move Deleter]]. Using his free service allows a Pokémon to forget one of its moves. This is especially useful for removing moves taught by [[HM]], as they would normally be permanent.

===A Berry A Day===
A Gentleman can be found taking a stroll in the northeast part of the city. Speak to him each day to receive a Berry. Possible varieties include {{b|Cheri}}, {{b|Chesto}}, {{b|Pecha}}, {{b|Rawst}}, {{b|Aspear}}, {{b|Leppa}}, {{b|Oran}}, {{b|Persim}}, {{b|Lum}}, and {{b|Sitrus}}. The type received is determined randomly.



